{"id":"deep:h03","prompt_preview":"A patch of lily pads doubles in size every day and covers the whole lake on day 48. On which day is the lak...","difficulty":0.2,"stakes":0.0,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":null,"rule_reason":null,"rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"deep","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":128,"gpu_seconds":1.1536},{"status":"done","tokens":136,"gpu_seconds":1.009},{"status":"done","tokens":151,"gpu_seconds":1.6977},{"status":"done","tokens":136,"gpu_seconds":1.4274},{"status":"done","tokens":141,"gpu_seconds":1.0126},{"status":"done","tokens":148,"gpu_seconds":1.6754},{"status":"done","tokens":131,"gpu_seconds":0.69},{"status":"done","tokens":286,"gpu_seconds":1.7645}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":[],"guardrail_verdicts":[],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"Let's go through the reasoning:\n\n- If the patch doubles in size every day, then one day before it’s completely full, it must have been half full.\n- It covers the whole lake on day 48.\n- Therefore, it was half covered on day 47.\n\nFinal answer: **Day 47**","correct":true,"latency_ms":18607,"total_tokens":1257,"total_gpu_seconds":10.4302,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831342.985023}
{"id":"deep:h01","prompt_preview":"A bat and a ball cost 1.10 pounds together. The bat costs 1.00 pound more than the ball. How many pence doe...","difficulty":0.7,"stakes":0.0,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":null,"rule_reason":null,"rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"deep","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":161,"gpu_seconds":0.8459},{"status":"done","tokens":172,"gpu_seconds":0.9256},{"status":"done","tokens":188,"gpu_seconds":1.2565},{"status":"done","tokens":187,"gpu_seconds":1.4466},{"status":"done","tokens":170,"gpu_seconds":1.6059},{"status":"done","tokens":179,"gpu_seconds":1.1044},{"status":"done","tokens":197,"gpu_seconds":1.338},{"status":"done","tokens":246,"gpu_seconds":24.083}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":[],"guardrail_verdicts":[],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"Let the ball cost \\( x \\) pence.  \nThen the bat costs \\( x + 100 \\) pence more than the ball.\n\nTogether:  \n\\( x + (x + 100) = 110 \\) pence.\n\nSo:  \n\\( 2x + 100 = 110 \\)  \n\\( 2x = 10 \\)  \n\\( x = 5 \\).\n\nThe ball costs 5 pence.\n\n**Final answer:** 5","correct":true,"latency_ms":37650,"total_tokens":1500,"total_gpu_seconds":32.6059,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831348.378528}
{"id":"deep:h04","prompt_preview":"I have two coins totalling 30p, and one of them is not a 20p coin. What is the value in pence of the larger...","difficulty":0.3,"stakes":0.0,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":null,"rule_reason":null,"rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"deep","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":476,"gpu_seconds":2.8509},{"status":"done","tokens":213,"gpu_seconds":1.512},{"status":"done","tokens":249,"gpu_seconds":1.8215},{"status":"done","tokens":245,"gpu_seconds":1.0881},{"status":"done","tokens":233,"gpu_seconds":2.0526},{"status":"done","tokens":286,"gpu_seconds":1.8485},{"status":"done","tokens":202,"gpu_seconds":1.3048},{"status":"done","tokens":653,"gpu_seconds":8.8481}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":[],"guardrail_verdicts":[],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"Let's go step by step.\n\n**Step 1 – Understanding the puzzle:**  \nYou have two coins totaling 30p.\n\n**Step 2 – Typical trick:**  \nOften, this is a variation of the “two coins totaling 30 cents and one is not a nickel” puzzle. In those puzzles, the trick is in the phrasing: “one of them is not [X]” means the *other* one *is*, but not necessarily the first.\n\n**Step 3 – Apply to this situation:**  \nWe are told one of them is **not** a 20p coin. That means: it’s possible that the *other* coin is a 20p coin, and the one that is \"not a 20p\" is something else.\n\n**Step 4 – Find coin values:**  \nIn Brit","correct":true,"latency_ms":20483,"total_tokens":2557,"total_gpu_seconds":21.3265,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831350.451623}
{"id":"deep:h02","prompt_preview":"If 5 machines take 5 minutes to make 5 widgets, how many minutes do 100 machines take to make 100 widgets?","difficulty":0.4,"stakes":0.0,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":null,"rule_reason":null,"rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"deep","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":275,"gpu_seconds":2.3581},{"status":"done","tokens":257,"gpu_seconds":1.2972},{"status":"done","tokens":286,"gpu_seconds":1.747},{"status":"done","tokens":213,"gpu_seconds":1.8153},{"status":"done","tokens":335,"gpu_seconds":1.8777},{"status":"done","tokens":321,"gpu_seconds":2.1648},{"status":"done","tokens":276,"gpu_seconds":1.9012},{"status":"done","tokens":446,"gpu_seconds":23.1345}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":[],"guardrail_verdicts":[],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"Let’s reason it through carefully.\n\n**Step 1 – Understand the given rate**  \nWe know:  \n5 machines → 5 minutes → 5 widgets.\n\nIf 5 machines make 5 widgets in 5 minutes, then each machine makes 1 widget in 5 minutes.  \nThis means each machine’s rate is \\( \\frac{1}{5} \\) widgets per minute.\n\n**Step 2 – Scale to 100 machines**  \nIf 1 machine makes 1 widget in 5 minutes, then 100 machines working together (each at that same rate) will make 100 widgets in **5 minutes**, because every machine independently makes 1 widget in 5 minutes.\n\nAlternatively: rate of 100 machines = \\(100 \\times \\frac{1}{5} = ","correct":true,"latency_ms":33765,"total_tokens":2409,"total_gpu_seconds":36.2958,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831352.370604}
{"id":"deep:h05","prompt_preview":"What is the sum of all integers from 1 to 100 that are divisible by 3?","difficulty":0.3,"stakes":0.1,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":null,"rule_reason":null,"rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"deep","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":411,"gpu_seconds":1.1176},{"status":"done","tokens":255,"gpu_seconds":1.7569},{"status":"done","tokens":279,"gpu_seconds":2.3221},{"status":"done","tokens":405,"gpu_seconds":2.0478},{"status":"done","tokens":300,"gpu_seconds":1.6862},{"status":"done","tokens":410,"gpu_seconds":2.2697},{"status":"done","tokens":355,"gpu_seconds":1.5684},{"status":"done","tokens":214,"gpu_seconds":17.1981}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":[],"guardrail_verdicts":[],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"Alright, let's work through the problem carefully.  \n\nWe want the sum of all integers from 1 to 100 that are divisible by 3.\n\n---\n\n**Step 1: Identify the sequence.**  \nThe integers divisible by 3 from 1 to 100 are:\n\\[\n3, 6, 9, \\dots, 99\n\\]\nThis is an arithmetic sequence where the first term \\(a_1 = 3\\), the last term \\(a_n = 99\\), and the common difference is \\(3\\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 2: Find the number of terms.**  \nSince these are multiples of 3, the \\(k\\)-th term is \\(3k\\). Set:\n\\[\n3k = 99\n\\]\n\\[\nk = 33\n\\]\nSo there are \\(33\\) terms.\n\n---\n\n**Step 3: Use the sum formula for an arithmetic sequence.**","correct":true,"latency_ms":29238,"total_tokens":2629,"total_gpu_seconds":29.9668,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831365.369309}
{"id":"deep:h07","prompt_preview":"How many trailing zeros does 25! (25 factorial) have?","difficulty":0.3,"stakes":0.1,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":null,"rule_reason":null,"rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"deep","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":230,"gpu_seconds":1.384},{"status":"done","tokens":384,"gpu_seconds":0.8259},{"status":"done","tokens":273,"gpu_seconds":1.2177},{"status":"done","tokens":385,"gpu_seconds":1.7345},{"status":"done","tokens":264,"gpu_seconds":3.0164},{"status":"done","tokens":429,"gpu_seconds":1.872},{"status":"done","tokens":222,"gpu_seconds":1.9451},{"status":"done","tokens":316,"gpu_seconds":6.6553}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":[],"guardrail_verdicts":[],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"We need to find how many trailing zeros are in \\(25!\\).  \nA trailing zero is created by a factor of 10, which is \\(2 \\times 5\\).  \nIn factorials, there are always more factors of 2 than 5, so we count the number of factors of 5 in \\(25!\\).\n\n**Step 1 – Count factors of 5**  \n\\(\\lfloor 25/5 \\rfloor = 5\\)  \n\\(\\lfloor 25/25 \\rfloor = 1\\)  \n\\(\\lfloor 25/125 \\rfloor = 0\\)  \n\nAdd them: \\(5 + 1 = 6\\).\n\n**Step 2 – Conclusion**  \nThere are 6 factors of 5, hence 6 factors of 10, hence 6 trailing zeros.\n\n**Final answer:**  \n\\[\n\\boxed{6}\n\\]","correct":true,"latency_ms":17796,"total_tokens":2503,"total_gpu_seconds":18.6509,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831370.3935978}
{"id":"deep:h08","prompt_preview":"In a room of 5 people, everyone shakes hands exactly once with everyone else. How many handshakes take place?","difficulty":0.1,"stakes":0.0,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":null,"rule_reason":null,"rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"deep","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":200,"gpu_seconds":1.2019},{"status":"done","tokens":292,"gpu_seconds":1.1044},{"status":"done","tokens":191,"gpu_seconds":1.0137},{"status":"done","tokens":260,"gpu_seconds":1.5879},{"status":"done","tokens":229,"gpu_seconds":1.859},{"status":"done","tokens":338,"gpu_seconds":2.4148},{"status":"done","tokens":143,"gpu_seconds":1.0217},{"status":"done","tokens":302,"gpu_seconds":8.2885}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":[],"guardrail_verdicts":[],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"Let's go step-by-step.\n\nWe have 5 people.  \nEach person shakes hands with every other person exactly once.  \n\nThat means this is a combination problem, because a handshake between two people is the same event regardless of who initiates it.\n\nThe number of handshakes is given by the formula for combinations:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{n}{2} = \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}\n\\]\n\nHere \\( n = 5 \\):\n\n\\[\n\\binom{5}{2} = \\frac{5 \\times 4}{2} = 10\n\\]\n\nSo, there are **10 handshakes**.\n\nFinal answer:  \n\\[\n\\boxed{10}\n\\]","correct":true,"latency_ms":17304,"total_tokens":1955,"total_gpu_seconds":18.4919,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831372.6687338}
{"id":"deep:h06","prompt_preview":"A train leaves at 14:47 and the journey takes 2 hours 38 minutes. What time does it arrive? Answer in 24-ho...","difficulty":0.15,"stakes":0.1,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":null,"rule_reason":null,"rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"deep","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":99,"gpu_seconds":1.1287},{"status":"done","tokens":197,"gpu_seconds":1.8343},{"status":"done","tokens":192,"gpu_seconds":1.3553},{"status":"done","tokens":162,"gpu_seconds":0.9046},{"status":"done","tokens":189,"gpu_seconds":2.0195},{"status":"done","tokens":176,"gpu_seconds":1.3892},{"status":"done","tokens":104,"gpu_seconds":0.7358},{"status":"done","tokens":191,"gpu_seconds":11.2616}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":[],"guardrail_verdicts":[],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"14:47 + 2 hours = 16:47.  \n16:47 + 38 minutes = 17:25.\n\n17:25","correct":true,"latency_ms":31999,"total_tokens":1310,"total_gpu_seconds":20.629,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831375.1160479}
{"id":"deep:s01","prompt_preview":"A paediatric patient weighs 18 kg. The prescribed dose is 15 mg/kg. What is the dose in mg?","difficulty":0.1,"stakes":0.9,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":null,"rule_reason":null,"rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"deep","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":71,"gpu_seconds":0.826},{"status":"done","tokens":105,"gpu_seconds":1.2714},{"status":"done","tokens":76,"gpu_seconds":0.8628},{"status":"done","tokens":131,"gpu_seconds":1.1223},{"status":"done","tokens":153,"gpu_seconds":1.9951},{"status":"done","tokens":71,"gpu_seconds":1.8043},{"status":"done","tokens":123,"gpu_seconds":1.6186},{"status":"done","tokens":139,"gpu_seconds":1.4136}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":[],"guardrail_verdicts":[],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"18 kg × 15 mg/kg = 270 mg.\n\n270","correct":true,"latency_ms":15141,"total_tokens":869,"total_gpu_seconds":10.9141,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831390.493631}
{"id":"deep:h10","prompt_preview":"A snail climbs 3 m up a 10 m well each day and slips back 2 m each night. On which day does it first reach ...","difficulty":0.65,"stakes":0.05,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":null,"rule_reason":null,"rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"deep","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":411,"gpu_seconds":1.9098},{"status":"done","tokens":431,"gpu_seconds":2.4793},{"status":"done","tokens":361,"gpu_seconds":1.6746},{"status":"done","tokens":340,"gpu_seconds":1.9978},{"status":"done","tokens":364,"gpu_seconds":2.1089},{"status":"done","tokens":318,"gpu_seconds":1.9538},{"status":"done","tokens":349,"gpu_seconds":1.8053},{"status":"done","tokens":382,"gpu_seconds":8.7327}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":[],"guardrail_verdicts":[],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"Let's reason through it step by step.\n\n---\n\n**Step 1 – Understanding the pattern**\n\nEach full day-night cycle:\n- Daytime: climbs +3 m  \n- Nighttime: slips –2 m  \n\nSo, net gain per full cycle = +1 m.  \nBut on the final day, the snail may reach the top before slipping back.\n\n---\n\n**Step 2 – Check the progress toward the top**\n\nWell depth = 10 m.\n\nAfter 1 full day and night:  \nStart 0 → climb to 3 → slip to 1 m.\n\nAfter day 2:  \n1 → climb to 4 → slip to 2 m.\n\nAfter day 3:  \n2 → climb to 5 → slip to 3 m.\n\nAfter day 4:  \n3 → climb to 6 → slip to 4 m.\n\nAfter day 5:  \n4 → climb to 7 → slip to 5 m.\n\nAf","correct":true,"latency_ms":31399,"total_tokens":2956,"total_gpu_seconds":22.6622,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831396.918014}
{"id":"deep:h09","prompt_preview":"What is the next number in the sequence 2, 6, 12, 20, 30, ?","difficulty":0.2,"stakes":0.1,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":null,"rule_reason":null,"rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"deep","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":246,"gpu_seconds":1.3163},{"status":"done","tokens":256,"gpu_seconds":1.3323},{"status":"done","tokens":226,"gpu_seconds":1.7777},{"status":"done","tokens":177,"gpu_seconds":1.122},{"status":"done","tokens":246,"gpu_seconds":1.675},{"status":"done","tokens":161,"gpu_seconds":1.7728},{"status":"done","tokens":239,"gpu_seconds":1.6344},{"status":"done","tokens":549,"gpu_seconds":28.6477}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":[],"guardrail_verdicts":[],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"Let's examine the sequence:  \n2, 6, 12, 20, 30, ?\n\nFirst, look at differences between terms:\n\n6 − 2 = 4  \n12 − 6 = 6  \n20 − 12 = 8  \n30 − 20 = 10  \n\nThe differences are increasing by 2 each time: 4, 6, 8, 10.\n\nNext difference would be 12.\n\nSo 30 + 12 = 42.\n\nAnother way: The terms are n(n+1) for n = 1, 2, 3, 4, 5,...  \n1×2 = 2, 2×3 = 6, 3×4 = 12, 4×5 = 20, 5×6 = 30, so next is 6×7 = 42.\n\nFinal answer:  \n**42**","correct":true,"latency_ms":40766,"total_tokens":2100,"total_gpu_seconds":39.2782,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831399.2800808}
{"id":"deep:s02","prompt_preview":"An invoice is 1,240 pounds net. Add UK VAT at 20%. What is the gross total in pounds?","difficulty":0.1,"stakes":0.3,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":null,"rule_reason":null,"rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"deep","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":103,"gpu_seconds":1.69},{"status":"done","tokens":118,"gpu_seconds":0.7808},{"status":"done","tokens":108,"gpu_seconds":1.3191},{"status":"done","tokens":110,"gpu_seconds":1.0244},{"status":"done","tokens":111,"gpu_seconds":0.6861},{"status":"done","tokens":117,"gpu_seconds":1.5752},{"status":"done","tokens":130,"gpu_seconds":1.349},{"status":"done","tokens":253,"gpu_seconds":12.368}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":[],"guardrail_verdicts":[],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"UK VAT at 20% on £1,240 is:\n\n1,240 × 0.20 = 248\n\nGross total:\n\n1,240 + 248 = 1,488\n\n£1,488","correct":true,"latency_ms":21896,"total_tokens":1050,"total_gpu_seconds":20.7926,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831401.530005}
{"id":"deep:s06","prompt_preview":"Insulin is dosed at 1 unit per 10 g of carbohydrate. A meal contains 85 g of carbohydrate. How many units, ...","difficulty":0.1,"stakes":0.85,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":null,"rule_reason":null,"rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"deep","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":132,"gpu_seconds":1.7699},{"status":"done","tokens":101,"gpu_seconds":0.8132},{"status":"done","tokens":136,"gpu_seconds":0.5942},{"status":"done","tokens":97,"gpu_seconds":0.9472},{"status":"done","tokens":126,"gpu_seconds":1.5658},{"status":"done","tokens":94,"gpu_seconds":1.5244},{"status":"done","tokens":159,"gpu_seconds":1.6199},{"status":"done","tokens":155,"gpu_seconds":1.3459}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":[],"guardrail_verdicts":[],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"Let's go step by step.\n\n- Dose: **1 unit per 10 g** carbohydrate.\n- Carbohydrate in meal: **85 g**.\n- Units needed: \\( 85 \\div 10 = 8.5 \\).\n\nTo one decimal place: **8.5**\n\n**8.5**","correct":true,"latency_ms":12259,"total_tokens":1000,"total_gpu_seconds":10.1805,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831417.580304}
{"id":"deep:s05","prompt_preview":"A payroll run covers 240 employees at 38.50 pounds per hour for 7.5 hours. What is the total cost in pounds?","difficulty":0.3,"stakes":0.3,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":null,"rule_reason":null,"rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"deep","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":286,"gpu_seconds":1.312},{"status":"done","tokens":332,"gpu_seconds":2.349},{"status":"done","tokens":266,"gpu_seconds":1.6554},{"status":"done","tokens":229,"gpu_seconds":1.7606},{"status":"done","tokens":316,"gpu_seconds":2.0472},{"status":"done","tokens":286,"gpu_seconds":2.0192},{"status":"done","tokens":211,"gpu_seconds":1.847},{"status":"done","tokens":342,"gpu_seconds":9.5024}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":[],"guardrail_verdicts":[],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"Let’s go through it step by step.\n\n1. **Hourly rate**: £38.50  \n2. **Hours per employee**: 7.5  \n3. **Number of employees**: 240  \n\nFirst, calculate the cost per employee:\n\n\\[\n38.50 \\times 7.5\n\\]\n\\[\n38.50 \\times 7 = 269.50\n\\]\n\\[\n38.50 \\times 0.5 = 19.25\n\\]\n\\[\n269.50 + 19.25 = 288.75\n\\]\nSo each employee costs £288.75.\n\nNow multiply by the number of employees:\n\n\\[\n288.75 \\times 240\n\\]\n\\[\n288.75 \\times 200 = 57,750\n\\]\n\\[\n288.75 \\times 40 = 11,550\n\\]\n\\[\n57,750 + 11,550 = 69,300\n\\]\n\nSo the total payroll cost is **£69,300**.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{69300}\n\\]","correct":true,"latency_ms":23448,"total_tokens":2268,"total_gpu_seconds":22.4928,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831425.125749}
{"id":"deep:s03","prompt_preview":"An infusion runs at 0.5 mg/kg/hour for a 72 kg adult. How many mg are delivered in 4 hours?","difficulty":0.1,"stakes":0.8,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":null,"rule_reason":null,"rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"deep","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":108,"gpu_seconds":0.9972},{"status":"done","tokens":108,"gpu_seconds":0.9056},{"status":"done","tokens":106,"gpu_seconds":0.9532},{"status":"done","tokens":108,"gpu_seconds":0.4644},{"status":"done","tokens":114,"gpu_seconds":1.5802},{"status":"done","tokens":110,"gpu_seconds":1.7004},{"status":"done","tokens":110,"gpu_seconds":1.405},{"status":"done","tokens":558,"gpu_seconds":30.2182}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":[],"guardrail_verdicts":[],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"First, calculate the dose rate:\n\n0.5 mg/kg/hour × 72 kg = 36 mg/hour.\n\nThen multiply by 4 hours:\n\n36 mg/hour × 4 hours = 144 mg.\n\n**144 mg**","correct":true,"latency_ms":44971,"total_tokens":1322,"total_gpu_seconds":38.2242,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831427.715733}
{"id":"deep:s04","prompt_preview":"A bridge cable is rated to 12,000 kg with a required safety factor of 4. What is the maximum working load i...","difficulty":0.1,"stakes":0.7,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":null,"rule_reason":null,"rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"deep","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":151,"gpu_seconds":1.8157},{"status":"done","tokens":128,"gpu_seconds":1.1973},{"status":"done","tokens":136,"gpu_seconds":1.2195},{"status":"done","tokens":212,"gpu_seconds":1.2813},{"status":"done","tokens":112,"gpu_seconds":1.2169},{"status":"done","tokens":133,"gpu_seconds":1.8176},{"status":"done","tokens":182,"gpu_seconds":1.9425},{"status":"done","tokens":259,"gpu_seconds":14.1119}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":[],"guardrail_verdicts":[],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"We need to apply the safety factor to the rated load.\n\nThe rated (breaking) load is 12,000 kg.  \nRequired safety factor = 4, meaning the working load must be 1/4 of the rated load.\n\n\\[\n\\text{Maximum working load} = \\frac{12{,}000}{4} = 3{,}000 \\text{ kg}\n\\]\n\nFinal answer: **3,000 kg**","correct":true,"latency_ms":39564,"total_tokens":1313,"total_gpu_seconds":24.6027,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831430.1801128}
{"id":"deep:s07","prompt_preview":"A loan of 20,000 pounds accrues 6% simple annual interest for 3 years. What is the total interest in pounds?","difficulty":0.1,"stakes":0.2,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":null,"rule_reason":null,"rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"deep","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":111,"gpu_seconds":1.3444},{"status":"done","tokens":143,"gpu_seconds":1.1124},{"status":"done","tokens":154,"gpu_seconds":1.4376},{"status":"done","tokens":108,"gpu_seconds":1.1161},{"status":"done","tokens":167,"gpu_seconds":1.8508},{"status":"done","tokens":167,"gpu_seconds":1.5759},{"status":"done","tokens":148,"gpu_seconds":1.2634},{"status":"done","tokens":200,"gpu_seconds":19.6826}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":[],"guardrail_verdicts":[],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"Simple interest = Principal × Rate × Time  \n= 20,000 × 0.06 × 3  \n= 20,000 × 0.18  \n= 3,600\n\nFinal answer: 3,600 pounds","correct":true,"latency_ms":36190,"total_tokens":1198,"total_gpu_seconds":29.3832,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831445.045533}
{"id":"deep:e11","prompt_preview":"How many bytes are in 4 kibibytes?","difficulty":0.2,"stakes":0.1,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":null,"rule_reason":null,"rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"deep","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":94,"gpu_seconds":1.4356},{"status":"done","tokens":91,"gpu_seconds":1.691},{"status":"done","tokens":130,"gpu_seconds":106.3983},{"status":"done","tokens":104,"gpu_seconds":1.0435},{"status":"done","tokens":109,"gpu_seconds":1.5848},{"status":"done","tokens":138,"gpu_seconds":1.8643},{"status":"done","tokens":119,"gpu_seconds":1.0225},{"status":"done","tokens":201,"gpu_seconds":33.0573}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":[],"guardrail_verdicts":[],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"Let’s go step by step.\n\n1 kibibyte (KiB) = 1024 bytes.  \n\nSo:  \n4 KiB × 1024 bytes/KiB = 4096 bytes.\n\n**Final answer:** 4096","correct":true,"latency_ms":145817,"total_tokens":986,"total_gpu_seconds":148.0973,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831450.785486}
{"id":"deep:s10","prompt_preview":"Paediatric paracetamol is 15 mg/kg, to a maximum of 4 doses in 24 hours. For a 12 kg child, what is the max...","difficulty":0.15,"stakes":0.85,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":null,"rule_reason":null,"rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"deep","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":232,"gpu_seconds":2.3458},{"status":"done","tokens":246,"gpu_seconds":1.3576},{"status":"done","tokens":239,"gpu_seconds":1.7733},{"status":"done","tokens":148,"gpu_seconds":0.7312},{"status":"done","tokens":252,"gpu_seconds":2.4065},{"status":"done","tokens":137,"gpu_seconds":1.5483},{"status":"done","tokens":184,"gpu_seconds":2.1201},{"status":"done","tokens":239,"gpu_seconds":8.385}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":[],"guardrail_verdicts":[],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"Let's go step by step.\n\n**Step 1 – Dose per kg**  \nThe dose is **15 mg/kg**.\n\n**Step 2 – Child’s weight**  \nThe child weighs **12 kg**.\n\n**Step 3 – Single dose calculation**  \n15 mg × 12 kg = **180 mg** per dose.\n\n**Step 4 – Maximum doses in 24 hours**  \nMaximum 4 doses in 24 hours.\n\n**Step 5 – Total over 24 hours**  \n180 mg × 4 = **720 mg**.\n\n**Step 6 – Check maximum limit**  \nThere is no stated total daily limit other than the 4-dose maximum, so 720 mg is the correct total from this regimen.\n\nFinal answer:\n\n**720 mg**","correct":true,"latency_ms":18353,"total_tokens":1677,"total_gpu_seconds":20.6678,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831452.88582}
{"id":"deep:s08","prompt_preview":"A coolant valve must close within 250 ms. The controller polls every 40 ms and the actuator takes 60 ms to ...","difficulty":0.5,"stakes":0.2,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":null,"rule_reason":null,"rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"deep","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":220,"gpu_seconds":1.9474},{"status":"done","tokens":183,"gpu_seconds":1.2899},{"status":"done","tokens":218,"gpu_seconds":1.1268},{"status":"done","tokens":158,"gpu_seconds":1.5082},{"status":"done","tokens":163,"gpu_seconds":1.7419},{"status":"done","tokens":224,"gpu_seconds":1.7258},{"status":"done","tokens":200,"gpu_seconds":1.6676},{"status":"done","tokens":329,"gpu_seconds":11.1358}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":[],"guardrail_verdicts":[],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"We need the worst-case response time from the moment a close command is required until the valve is fully closed.\n\nBreakdown:\n- Polling interval: every 40 ms. Worst case, the command just misses a poll, so wait up to 40 ms for the next poll.\n- Actuator movement time: 60 ms.\n- Controller processing time isn’t mentioned separately, so assume it’s included in the polling/actuation or negligible.\n\nWorst-case response time = polling delay + actuator time  \n= 40 ms + 60 ms = 100 ms.\n\n250 ms is the requirement, but the question asks for the worst-case response time. That’s 100 ms.\n\nFinal answer: 100 ","correct":true,"latency_ms":37364,"total_tokens":1695,"total_gpu_seconds":22.1434,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831455.1211672}
{"id":"deep:s09","prompt_preview":"The VAT registration threshold is 85,000 pounds. A business has turned over 84,200 pounds and then issues a...","difficulty":0.1,"stakes":0.3,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":null,"rule_reason":null,"rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"deep","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":167,"gpu_seconds":2.6517},{"status":"done","tokens":102,"gpu_seconds":0.9315},{"status":"done","tokens":156,"gpu_seconds":1.3635},{"status":"done","tokens":112,"gpu_seconds":1.5881},{"status":"done","tokens":171,"gpu_seconds":1.6631},{"status":"done","tokens":158,"gpu_seconds":2.0481},{"status":"done","tokens":158,"gpu_seconds":0.9827},{"status":"done","tokens":283,"gpu_seconds":13.1162}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":[],"guardrail_verdicts":[],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"Let’s go through it carefully.\n\nThe VAT registration threshold is £85,000.\n\nThe business has already turned over £84,200.\n\nThen it issues a further invoice of £1,100.\n\nSo the new turnover = £84,200 + £1,100 = £85,300.\n\n£85,300 is greater than £85,000, so yes, it now exceeds the threshold.\n\n**Answer: yes**","correct":true,"latency_ms":26880,"total_tokens":1307,"total_gpu_seconds":24.3449,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831457.21747}
{"id":"deep:x03","prompt_preview":"Write a Python function `is_safe_dose(weight_kg, mg)` that returns True if and only if mg is at most 15 mg ...","difficulty":0.1,"stakes":0.8,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":null,"rule_reason":null,"rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"deep","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":104,"gpu_seconds":1.3299},{"status":"done","tokens":104,"gpu_seconds":1.1245},{"status":"done","tokens":104,"gpu_seconds":3.5439},{"status":"done","tokens":104,"gpu_seconds":1.6742},{"status":"done","tokens":104,"gpu_seconds":0.8845},{"status":"done","tokens":104,"gpu_seconds":0.9741},{"status":"done","tokens":104,"gpu_seconds":0.952}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":[],"guardrail_verdicts":[],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"```python\ndef is_safe_dose(weight_kg, mg):\n    return mg <= 15 * weight_kg\n```","correct":true,"latency_ms":17464,"total_tokens":728,"total_gpu_seconds":10.4831,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831474.9171882}
{"id":"deep:x04","prompt_preview":"Write a Python function `parse_amount(s)` that converts a string like '£1,234.50' into the float 1234.5. It...","difficulty":0.2,"stakes":0.2,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":null,"rule_reason":null,"rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"deep","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":148,"gpu_seconds":0.5722},{"status":"done","tokens":125,"gpu_seconds":1.1012},{"status":"done","tokens":153,"gpu_seconds":0.7156},{"status":"done","tokens":133,"gpu_seconds":1.062},{"status":"done","tokens":145,"gpu_seconds":1.6817},{"status":"done","tokens":133,"gpu_seconds":0.8343},{"status":"done","tokens":152,"gpu_seconds":1.2361}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":[],"guardrail_verdicts":[],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"```python\ndef parse_amount(s):\n    if not isinstance(s, str) or not s.strip():\n        raise ValueError(\"empty or blank string\")\n    cleaned = s.replace('£', '').replace('$', '').replace('€', '').replace(',', '').strip()\n    return float(cleaned)\n```","correct":true,"latency_ms":17425,"total_tokens":989,"total_gpu_seconds":7.2031,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831479.96507}
{"id":"deep:x05","prompt_preview":"Write a Python function `median(xs)` returning the median of a list of numbers, averaging the middle two fo...","difficulty":0.1,"stakes":0.1,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":null,"rule_reason":null,"rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"deep","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":150,"gpu_seconds":0.5355},{"status":"done","tokens":150,"gpu_seconds":1.1005},{"status":"done","tokens":150,"gpu_seconds":1.1278},{"status":"done","tokens":150,"gpu_seconds":1.2999},{"status":"done","tokens":153,"gpu_seconds":1.2085},{"status":"done","tokens":150,"gpu_seconds":0.5185},{"status":"done","tokens":150,"gpu_seconds":1.5737}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":[],"guardrail_verdicts":[],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"```python\ndef median(xs):\n    if not xs:\n        raise ValueError(\"median() arg is an empty sequence\")\n    s = sorted(xs)\n    n = len(s)\n    mid = n // 2\n    if n % 2:\n        return s[mid]\n    return (s[mid - 1] + s[mid]) / 2\n```","correct":true,"latency_ms":29177,"total_tokens":1053,"total_gpu_seconds":7.3644,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831494.638379}
{"id":"deep:x06","prompt_preview":"Write a Python function `binary_search(xs, target)` over a sorted list that returns the index of target or ...","difficulty":0.1,"stakes":0.1,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":null,"rule_reason":null,"rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"deep","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":167,"gpu_seconds":1.8526},{"status":"done","tokens":165,"gpu_seconds":0.8991},{"status":"done","tokens":165,"gpu_seconds":0.4714},{"status":"done","tokens":165,"gpu_seconds":1.0664},{"status":"done","tokens":165,"gpu_seconds":0.8381},{"status":"done","tokens":165,"gpu_seconds":1.6236},{"status":"done","tokens":165,"gpu_seconds":2.4717}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":[],"guardrail_verdicts":[],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"```python\ndef binary_search(xs, target):\n    lo, hi = 0, len(xs) - 1\n    while lo <= hi:\n        mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n        if xs[mid] == target:\n            return mid\n        elif xs[mid] < target:\n            lo = mid + 1\n        else:\n            hi = mid - 1\n    return -1\n```","correct":true,"latency_ms":31004,"total_tokens":1157,"total_gpu_seconds":9.2229,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831499.2537751}
{"id":"deep:x07","prompt_preview":"Write a Python function `apply_vat(net, rate)` returning the gross amount rounded to two decimal places, ro...","difficulty":0.55,"stakes":0.6,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":null,"rule_reason":null,"rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"deep","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":149,"gpu_seconds":1.1118},{"status":"done","tokens":149,"gpu_seconds":1.39},{"status":"done","tokens":169,"gpu_seconds":0.8407},{"status":"done","tokens":149,"gpu_seconds":0.89},{"status":"done","tokens":148,"gpu_seconds":1.0357},{"status":"done","tokens":149,"gpu_seconds":1.2796},{"status":"done","tokens":149,"gpu_seconds":1.4405}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":[],"guardrail_verdicts":[],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"```python\ndef apply_vat(net, rate):\n    from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_UP\n    gross = Decimal(str(net)) * (Decimal('1') + Decimal(str(rate)))\n    return float(gross.quantize(Decimal('0.01'), rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP))\n```","correct":true,"latency_ms":23230,"total_tokens":1062,"total_gpu_seconds":7.9883,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831503.430969}
{"id":"deep:x08","prompt_preview":"Write a Python function `check_transfer(balance, amount)` that returns the string 'ok' when amount is posit...","difficulty":0.1,"stakes":0.1,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":null,"rule_reason":null,"rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"deep","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":106,"gpu_seconds":1.3339},{"status":"done","tokens":108,"gpu_seconds":0.5409},{"status":"done","tokens":108,"gpu_seconds":0.7291},{"status":"done","tokens":108,"gpu_seconds":0.9253},{"status":"done","tokens":111,"gpu_seconds":0.96},{"status":"done","tokens":106,"gpu_seconds":1.4198},{"status":"done","tokens":106,"gpu_seconds":1.7358}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":[],"guardrail_verdicts":[],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"```python\ndef check_transfer(balance, amount):\n    return 'ok' if 0 < amount <= balance else 'rejected'\n```","correct":true,"latency_ms":22595,"total_tokens":753,"total_gpu_seconds":7.6448,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831507.82163}
{"id":"deep:x01","prompt_preview":"An aircraft burns 2.4 kg of fuel per km and must carry a 400 kg reserve. What is the required fuel load in ...","difficulty":0.1,"stakes":0.2,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":null,"rule_reason":null,"rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"deep","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":206,"gpu_seconds":1.4455},{"status":"done","tokens":264,"gpu_seconds":1.381},{"status":"done","tokens":233,"gpu_seconds":0.8423},{"status":"done","tokens":198,"gpu_seconds":1.3417},{"status":"done","tokens":242,"gpu_seconds":1.6954},{"status":"done","tokens":243,"gpu_seconds":2.1231},{"status":"done","tokens":209,"gpu_seconds":1.6771},{"status":"done","tokens":203,"gpu_seconds":60.2793}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":[],"guardrail_verdicts":[],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"Let's go step-by-step.\n\n**Step 1: Fuel needed for the flight itself**  \nBurn rate: 2.4 kg/km  \nDistance: 1,850 km  \nFuel for trip = \\( 2.4 \\times 1850 \\)  \n\\( 2.4 \\times 1850 = 4440 \\) kg.\n\n**Step 2: Add reserve**  \nReserve: 400 kg  \nTotal fuel = \\( 4440 + 400 = 4840 \\) kg.\n\n**Step 3: Check units and logic**  \nFuel load in kg — yes, straightforward.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{4840}\n\\]","correct":true,"latency_ms":73609,"total_tokens":1798,"total_gpu_seconds":70.7854,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831511.2935848}
{"id":"deep:x02","prompt_preview":"A ledger has three entries: +12,450.20, -8,199.99 and -1,000.01 pounds. What is the closing balance in poun...","difficulty":0.1,"stakes":0.2,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":null,"rule_reason":null,"rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"deep","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":195,"gpu_seconds":2.0595},{"status":"done","tokens":225,"gpu_seconds":1.0015},{"status":"done","tokens":201,"gpu_seconds":1.2028},{"status":"done","tokens":187,"gpu_seconds":2.1714},{"status":"done","tokens":165,"gpu_seconds":1.0638},{"status":"done","tokens":186,"gpu_seconds":1.9945},{"status":"done","tokens":185,"gpu_seconds":1.6986},{"status":"done","tokens":332,"gpu_seconds":40.8662}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":[],"guardrail_verdicts":[],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"First, write the entries with signs:\n\n+12,450.20  \n-8,199.99  \n-1,000.01  \n\nStep 1: Add the negatives together.\n\n8,199.99 + 1,000.01 = 9,200.00 exactly.\n\nStep 2: Subtract the total negatives from the positive entry.\n\n12,450.20 − 9,200.00 = 3,250.20.\n\nStep 3: Check decimal places — already two decimal places.\n\nFinal balance = 3,250.20 pounds.\n\n3,250.20","correct":true,"latency_ms":68820,"total_tokens":1676,"total_gpu_seconds":52.0583,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831513.9988291}
