{"id":"ponder:h01","prompt_preview":"A bat and a ball cost 1.10 pounds together. The bat costs 1.00 pound more than the ball. How many pence doe...","difficulty":0.7,"stakes":0.1,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":null,"rule_reason":null,"rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"ponder","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":177,"gpu_seconds":1.4586},{"status":"done","tokens":205,"gpu_seconds":1.4557},{"status":"done","tokens":189,"gpu_seconds":0.6114},{"status":"done","tokens":195,"gpu_seconds":1.8521},{"status":"done","tokens":201,"gpu_seconds":1.1467}],"sandbox_ran":false,"sandbox_passed":null,"guardrails":[],"guardrail_verdicts":[],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"Let the ball cost \\(x\\) pence.\n\nThe bat costs 1.00 pound more than the ball, so the bat costs \\(x + 100\\) pence.\n\nTogether they cost 1.10 pounds, which is 110 pence:\n\n\\[\nx + (x + 100) = 110\n\\]\n\n\\[\n2x + 100 = 110\n\\]\n\n\\[\n2x = 10\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx = 5\n\\]\n\nSo the ball costs 5 pence.\n\n**5**","correct":true,"latency_ms":20631,"total_tokens":967,"total_gpu_seconds":6.5245,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831569.3622131}
