{"id":"ponder:h10","prompt_preview":"A snail climbs 3 m up a 10 m well each day and slips back 2 m each night. On which day does it first reach ...","difficulty":0.65,"stakes":0.05,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":null,"rule_reason":null,"rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"ponder","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":326,"gpu_seconds":1.8913},{"status":"done","tokens":341,"gpu_seconds":1.5623},{"status":"done","tokens":422,"gpu_seconds":1.8655},{"status":"done","tokens":367,"gpu_seconds":2.3408},{"status":"done","tokens":356,"gpu_seconds":1.7031}],"sandbox_ran":false,"sandbox_passed":null,"guardrails":[],"guardrail_verdicts":[],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"Let’s go through it step-by-step.\n\n**Day 1:**  \nClimbs 3 m → at 3 m.  \nSlips 2 m at night → at 1 m.\n\n**Day 2:**  \nClimbs to 4 m (1 + 3).  \nSlips to 2 m at night.\n\n**Day 3:**  \nClimbs to 5 m.  \nSlips to 3 m at night.\n\n**Day 4:**  \nClimbs to 6 m.  \nSlips to 4 m at night.\n\n**Day 5:**  \nClimbs to 7 m.  \nSlips to 5 m at night.\n\n**Day 6:**  \nClimbs to 8 m.  \nSlips to 6 m at night.\n\n**Day 7:**  \nClimbs to 9 m.  \nSlips to 7 m at night.\n\n**Day 8:**  \nAt start of the day: 7 m.  \nClimbs 3 m → 10 m, **which is the top**.\n\nIt reaches the top on the **8th day**, and doesn’t slip back because it’s already ou","correct":true,"latency_ms":14989,"total_tokens":1812,"total_gpu_seconds":9.363,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831596.441706}
