{"id":"ponder:s07","prompt_preview":"A loan of 20,000 pounds accrues 6% simple annual interest for 3 years. What is the total interest in pounds?","difficulty":0.1,"stakes":0.1,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":"financial_total","rule_reason":"Financial totals are always deep-verified regardless of apparent difficulty. (the score alone would have spent cheap)","rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"ponder","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":158,"gpu_seconds":1.156},{"status":"done","tokens":170,"gpu_seconds":1.6999},{"status":"done","tokens":169,"gpu_seconds":1.2784},{"status":"done","tokens":107,"gpu_seconds":1.3021},{"status":"done","tokens":143,"gpu_seconds":1.7143},{"status":"done","tokens":240,"gpu_seconds":8.4119}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":["numeric_answer_present","no_hedging","no_personal_data"],"guardrail_verdicts":[{"name":"numeric_answer_present","outcome":"allow","detail":""},{"name":"no_hedging","outcome":"allow","detail":""},{"name":"no_personal_data","outcome":"allow","detail":""}],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"We need simple interest:  \n\\( I = P \\times r \\times t \\)  \n\\( P = 20{,}000 \\)  \n\\( r = 0.06 \\)  \n\\( t = 3 \\)  \n\n\\( I = 20{,}000 \\times 0.06 \\times 3 \\)  \n\\( = 1{,}200 \\times 3 \\)  \n\\( = 3{,}600 \\)  \n\nFinal answer: **3,600 pounds**","correct":true,"latency_ms":23460,"total_tokens":987,"total_gpu_seconds":15.5626,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831640.3614771}
{"id":"ponder:s08","prompt_preview":"A coolant valve must close within 250 ms. The controller polls every 40 ms and the actuator takes 60 ms to ...","difficulty":0.3,"stakes":0.2,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":"safety_margin","rule_reason":"Load, tolerance and timing margins are verified by execution -- a plausible-looking number is the failure mode here. (the score alone would have spent cheap)","rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"ponder","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":303,"gpu_seconds":2.4607},{"status":"done","tokens":283,"gpu_seconds":2.2947},{"status":"done","tokens":213,"gpu_seconds":1.3829},{"status":"done","tokens":165,"gpu_seconds":1.0894},{"status":"done","tokens":354,"gpu_seconds":1.7554},{"status":"done","tokens":268,"gpu_seconds":10.2102}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":["numeric_answer_present","units_present","no_hedging"],"guardrail_verdicts":[{"name":"numeric_answer_present","outcome":"allow","detail":""},{"name":"units_present","outcome":"allow","detail":""},{"name":"no_hedging","outcome":"allow","detail":""}],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"Let's reason through the problem step by step.\n\n**Step 1 – Understanding the components of delay**  \n- The controller polls every **40 ms**. In the worst case, the event occurs just after a poll, so the controller waits almost the full polling interval before noticing: **40 ms**.  \n- The actuator takes **60 ms** to move once commanded.\n\n**Step 2 – Worst-case response time**  \nWorst-case response time = polling delay + actuator movement time  \n= 40 ms + 60 ms = **100 ms**.\n\n**Step 3 – Additional delays?**  \nNo other delay mentioned (no computation delay, transmission delay, etc.), so we stick t","correct":true,"latency_ms":21686,"total_tokens":1586,"total_gpu_seconds":19.1933,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831642.275181}
{"id":"ponder:s05","prompt_preview":"A payroll run covers 240 employees at 38.50 pounds per hour for 7.5 hours. What is the total cost in pounds?","difficulty":0.1,"stakes":0.3,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":"financial_total","rule_reason":"Financial totals are always deep-verified regardless of apparent difficulty. (the score alone would have spent cheap)","rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"ponder","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":274,"gpu_seconds":1.1323},{"status":"done","tokens":230,"gpu_seconds":1.4411},{"status":"done","tokens":246,"gpu_seconds":1.7562},{"status":"done","tokens":193,"gpu_seconds":4.9369},{"status":"done","tokens":300,"gpu_seconds":2.3494},{"status":"done","tokens":745,"gpu_seconds":12.9303}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":["numeric_answer_present","no_hedging","no_personal_data"],"guardrail_verdicts":[{"name":"numeric_answer_present","outcome":"allow","detail":""},{"name":"no_hedging","outcome":"allow","detail":""},{"name":"no_personal_data","outcome":"allow","detail":""}],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"Let’s go step by step.\n\n1. **Hourly rate per employee:** £38.50  \n2. **Hours worked per employee:** 7.5  \n3. **Cost per employee:**  \n   \\( 38.50 \\times 7.5 \\)  \n   - \\( 38.50 \\times 7 = 269.50 \\)  \n   - \\( 38.50 \\times 0.5 = 19.25 \\)  \n   - Total = \\( 269.50 + 19.25 = 288.75 \\)\n\n4. **Total for 240 employees:**  \n   \\( 288.75 \\times 240 \\)  \n   - \\( 288.75 \\times 200 = 57,750 \\)  \n   - \\( 288.75 \\times 40 = 11,550 \\)  \n   - Total = \\( 57,750 + 11,550 = 69,300 \\)\n\n**Final answer:**  \n\\[\n\\boxed{69300}\n\\]","correct":true,"latency_ms":39834,"total_tokens":1988,"total_gpu_seconds":24.5462,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831644.345524}
{"id":"ponder:s04","prompt_preview":"A bridge cable is rated to 12,000 kg with a required safety factor of 4. What is the maximum working load i...","difficulty":0.1,"stakes":0.7,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":"safety_margin","rule_reason":"Load, tolerance and timing margins are verified by execution -- a plausible-looking number is the failure mode here.","rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"ponder","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":151,"gpu_seconds":1.2442},{"status":"done","tokens":181,"gpu_seconds":1.968},{"status":"done","tokens":151,"gpu_seconds":1.6354},{"status":"done","tokens":157,"gpu_seconds":1.1403},{"status":"done","tokens":149,"gpu_seconds":1.7031},{"status":"done","tokens":164,"gpu_seconds":2.9143},{"status":"done","tokens":136,"gpu_seconds":1.2667},{"status":"done","tokens":381,"gpu_seconds":15.2956}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":["numeric_answer_present","units_present","no_hedging"],"guardrail_verdicts":[{"name":"numeric_answer_present","outcome":"allow","detail":""},{"name":"units_present","outcome":"allow","detail":""},{"name":"no_hedging","outcome":"allow","detail":""}],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"We need the maximum working load given:\n\n- Rated (breaking) capacity = 12,000 kg  \n- Required safety factor = 4  \n\nThe working load is:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Working load} = \\frac{\\text{Rated capacity}}{\\text{Safety factor}}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= \\frac{12,000}{4} = 3,000 \\text{ kg}\n\\]\n\nFinal answer: **3,000 kg**","correct":true,"latency_ms":48935,"total_tokens":1470,"total_gpu_seconds":27.1676,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831646.101803}
{"id":"ponder:x03","prompt_preview":"Write a Python function `is_safe_dose(weight_kg, mg)` that returns True if and only if mg is at most 15 mg ...","difficulty":0.1,"stakes":0.8,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":"clinical_dose","rule_reason":"Dosing arithmetic is recomputed and executed before it is trusted, however simple the sum looks.","rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"ponder","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":104,"gpu_seconds":1.2505},{"status":"done","tokens":104,"gpu_seconds":0.7349},{"status":"done","tokens":104,"gpu_seconds":0.663},{"status":"done","tokens":104,"gpu_seconds":1.1229},{"status":"done","tokens":104,"gpu_seconds":1.6311},{"status":"done","tokens":104,"gpu_seconds":1.2902},{"status":"done","tokens":104,"gpu_seconds":1.5081}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":["numeric_answer_present","units_present","no_hedging"],"guardrail_verdicts":[{"name":"numeric_answer_present","outcome":"allow","detail":""},{"name":"units_present","outcome":"allow","detail":""},{"name":"no_hedging","outcome":"allow","detail":""}],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"```python\ndef is_safe_dose(weight_kg, mg):\n    return mg <= 15 * weight_kg\n```","correct":true,"latency_ms":13027,"total_tokens":728,"total_gpu_seconds":8.2007,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831666.7039402}
{"id":"ponder:s09","prompt_preview":"The VAT registration threshold is 85,000 pounds. A business has turned over 84,200 pounds and then issues a...","difficulty":0.05,"stakes":0.3,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":"financial_total","rule_reason":"Financial totals are always deep-verified regardless of apparent difficulty. (the score alone would have spent cheap)","rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"ponder","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":179,"gpu_seconds":1.7333},{"status":"done","tokens":157,"gpu_seconds":1.496},{"status":"done","tokens":158,"gpu_seconds":0.8021},{"status":"done","tokens":154,"gpu_seconds":0.8125},{"status":"done","tokens":164,"gpu_seconds":1.2001},{"status":"done","tokens":264,"gpu_seconds":33.207}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":["numeric_answer_present","no_hedging","no_personal_data"],"guardrail_verdicts":[{"name":"numeric_answer_present","outcome":"allow","detail":""},{"name":"no_hedging","outcome":"allow","detail":""},{"name":"no_personal_data","outcome":"allow","detail":""}],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"Let's break this down step by step.\n\n- The VAT registration threshold is £85,000.\n- The business has already turned over £84,200.\n- It then issues a further invoice for £1,100.\n\nFirst, add the new invoice to the previous turnover:\n\n£84,200 + £1,100 = £85,300.\n\n£85,300 is greater than £85,000.  \nSo yes, it now exceeds the threshold.\n\n**Final answer:** Yes.","correct":true,"latency_ms":48377,"total_tokens":1076,"total_gpu_seconds":39.251,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831673.510977}
{"id":"ponder:s10","prompt_preview":"Paediatric paracetamol is 15 mg/kg, to a maximum of 4 doses in 24 hours. For a 12 kg child, what is the max...","difficulty":0.15,"stakes":0.85,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":"clinical_dose","rule_reason":"Dosing arithmetic is recomputed and executed before it is trusted, however simple the sum looks.","rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"ponder","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":234,"gpu_seconds":1.9151},{"status":"done","tokens":165,"gpu_seconds":1.1107},{"status":"done","tokens":215,"gpu_seconds":1.6051},{"status":"done","tokens":236,"gpu_seconds":1.6627},{"status":"done","tokens":228,"gpu_seconds":1.5279},{"status":"done","tokens":250,"gpu_seconds":1.6108},{"status":"done","tokens":235,"gpu_seconds":1.5277},{"status":"done","tokens":261,"gpu_seconds":14.8555}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":["numeric_answer_present","units_present","no_hedging"],"guardrail_verdicts":[{"name":"numeric_answer_present","outcome":"allow","detail":""},{"name":"units_present","outcome":"allow","detail":""},{"name":"no_hedging","outcome":"allow","detail":""}],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"Let's go step by step.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate dose per administration.**  \nThe dose is 15 mg/kg.  \nChild's weight = 12 kg.  \nDose per administration = 15 × 12 = 180 mg.\n\n**Step 2: Determine number of doses per 24 hours.**  \nMaximum is 4 doses in 24 hours.\n\n**Step 3: Calculate total maximum dose over 24 hours.**  \nTotal = 180 mg × 4 = 720 mg.\n\n**Step 4: Check against maximum daily limit.**  \nThe problem doesn't give an explicit separate maximum daily mg limit other than the 4-dose rule, so 720 mg is the answer based on weight and dosing frequency.\n\n**Final answer:**  \n720 mg","correct":true,"latency_ms":44115,"total_tokens":1824,"total_gpu_seconds":25.8155,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831678.430067}
{"id":"ponder:x01","prompt_preview":"An aircraft burns 2.4 kg of fuel per km and must carry a 400 kg reserve. What is the required fuel load in ...","difficulty":0.1,"stakes":0.3,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":"safety_margin","rule_reason":"Load, tolerance and timing margins are verified by execution -- a plausible-looking number is the failure mode here. (the score alone would have spent cheap)","rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"ponder","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":207,"gpu_seconds":0.9476},{"status":"done","tokens":253,"gpu_seconds":1.0821},{"status":"done","tokens":214,"gpu_seconds":1.2865},{"status":"done","tokens":222,"gpu_seconds":1.2832},{"status":"done","tokens":273,"gpu_seconds":1.9358},{"status":"done","tokens":509,"gpu_seconds":16.8295}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":["numeric_answer_present","units_present","no_hedging"],"guardrail_verdicts":[{"name":"numeric_answer_present","outcome":"allow","detail":""},{"name":"units_present","outcome":"allow","detail":""},{"name":"no_hedging","outcome":"allow","detail":""}],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"Let's go step-by-step.\n\n---\n\n**Step 1: Fuel burned for the flight distance**  \nBurn rate: 2.4 kg/km  \nDistance: 1,850 km  \n\nFuel burned = \\( 2.4 \\times 1850 \\)  \n\\( 2.4 \\times 1850 = 4440 \\) kg.\n\n---\n\n**Step 2: Add reserve fuel**  \nReserve = 400 kg  \n\nTotal fuel = \\( 4440 + 400 = 4840 \\) kg.\n\n---\n\n**Step 3: Conclusion**  \nThe required fuel load is 4840 kg.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{4840}\n\\]","correct":true,"latency_ms":33956,"total_tokens":1678,"total_gpu_seconds":23.3647,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831680.218577}
