{"id":"ponder:ask31918103","prompt_preview":"what is the perplexity of AI models","difficulty":0.2,"stakes":0.1,"budget":"cheap","matched_rule":null,"rule_reason":null,"rule_id":"ponder-cheap-answer-only","strategy":"ponder","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":385,"gpu_seconds":1.8827}],"sandbox_ran":false,"sandbox_passed":null,"guardrails":[],"guardrail_verdicts":[],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"Perplexity is a metric for how “surprised” or uncertain a language model is when predicting text. It is defined as the exponential of the average negative log-likelihood the model assigns to a sequence:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Perplexity} = \\exp\\left(-\\frac{1}{N}\\sum_{i=1}^{N}\\log P(w_i \\mid w_{<i})\\right)\n\\]\n\nLower perplexity means the model predicts the text better. Intuitively, it can be interpreted as the effective number of equally likely choices the model is choosing among at each step.\n\nImportant caveats:\n- It depends heavily on the dataset, tokenizer, and vocabulary.\n- Values are not comparable acro","correct":null,"latency_ms":5679,"total_tokens":385,"total_gpu_seconds":1.8827,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789831923.810242}
{"id":"ponder:ask32003901","prompt_preview":"An invoice of 1029.00 has VAT at 20%. What is the gross total?","difficulty":0.2,"stakes":0.3,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":"financial_total","rule_reason":"Financial totals are always deep-verified regardless of apparent difficulty. (the score alone would have spent cheap)","rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"ponder","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":235,"gpu_seconds":4.4511},{"status":"done","tokens":262,"gpu_seconds":3.2303},{"status":"done","tokens":274,"gpu_seconds":3.1498},{"status":"done","tokens":246,"gpu_seconds":2.6739},{"status":"done","tokens":300,"gpu_seconds":2.6195},{"status":"done","tokens":415,"gpu_seconds":1.7132}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":["numeric_answer_present","no_hedging","no_personal_data"],"guardrail_verdicts":[{"name":"numeric_answer_present","outcome":"allow","detail":""},{"name":"no_hedging","outcome":"allow","detail":""},{"name":"no_personal_data","outcome":"allow","detail":""}],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"Gross total = 1029.00 + 20% VAT  \nVAT = 1029.00 × 0.20 = 205.80  \nGross total = 1029.00 + 205.80 = **1234.80**","correct":null,"latency_ms":18371,"total_tokens":1732,"total_gpu_seconds":17.8378,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789832022.293472}
{"id":"ponder:ask33643652","prompt_preview":"please can you talk about peanut butter?","difficulty":0.0,"stakes":0.0,"budget":"cheap","matched_rule":null,"rule_reason":null,"rule_id":"ponder-cheap-answer-only","strategy":"ponder","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":411,"gpu_seconds":2.4599}],"sandbox_ran":false,"sandbox_passed":null,"guardrails":[],"guardrail_verdicts":[],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"Peanut butter is a spread made from ground roasted peanuts. It’s usually creamy or crunchy, and often contains added salt, sugar, and stabilizers like hydrogenated vegetable oil to keep it from separating. Natural peanut butter typically has just peanuts and maybe salt, so the oil separates and needs stirring.\n\nIt’s a good source of plant protein, healthy fats, vitamin E, niacin, and magnesium, though it’s calorie-dense. A typical 2-tablespoon serving has about 180–200 calories, 7–8 grams of protein, and 15–16 grams of fat. It’s popular in sandwiches, smoothies, sauces, baking, and satay dishe","correct":null,"latency_ms":5821,"total_tokens":411,"total_gpu_seconds":2.4599,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789833649.496595}
{"id":"ponder:ask34708146","prompt_preview":"A child weighs 24 kg. Amoxicillin is 20 mg/kg per dose. What is a single dose in mg?","difficulty":0.1,"stakes":0.8,"budget":"deep","matched_rule":"paediatric_dose","rule_reason":"Weight-based paediatric dosing is recomputed and executed before it is trusted. A tenfold slip here is the most-reported fatal medication error, and the arithmetic always looks trivial.","rule_id":"ponder-deep-reason","strategy":"ponder","samples":[{"status":"done","tokens":89,"gpu_seconds":2.303},{"status":"done","tokens":74,"gpu_seconds":1.2452},{"status":"done","tokens":78,"gpu_seconds":1.0067},{"status":"done","tokens":84,"gpu_seconds":0.7665},{"status":"done","tokens":83,"gpu_seconds":0.9},{"status":"done","tokens":76,"gpu_seconds":1.2839},{"status":"done","tokens":90,"gpu_seconds":1.5264},{"status":"done","tokens":199,"gpu_seconds":0.7705}],"sandbox_ran":true,"sandbox_passed":true,"guardrails":["health_topics_only","numeric_answer_present","units_present","safe_dose_notation","no_hedging"],"guardrail_verdicts":[{"name":"numeric_answer_present","outcome":"allow","detail":""},{"name":"units_present","outcome":"allow","detail":""},{"name":"safe_dose_notation","outcome":"allow","detail":""},{"name":"no_hedging","outcome":"allow","detail":""}],"guardrail_escalated":false,"guardrail_blocked":false,"answer":"24 kg × 20 mg/kg = 480 mg  \n(since kg cancels out: 24 × 20 = 480)\n\n480","correct":null,"latency_ms":10665,"total_tokens":773,"total_gpu_seconds":9.8022,"logfire_trace_url":null,"status":"done","ts":1789834718.833982}
